# Quarto build artifacts ------------------------------------------------------

# Internal render cache and project scratch.
/.quarto/

# Rendered website output -- you deploy this, no need to track it.
/_site/

# Per-document asset folders Quarto extracts on render (figures, libs, etc.),
# e.g. posts/<slug>/index_files/figure-html/. Matches at any depth.
*_files/

# Intermediate notebooks Quarto writes while executing a .qmd.
*.quarto_ipynb

# Jupyter execution caches / checkpoints.
.jupyter_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Keep /_freeze/ COMMITTED ----------------------------------------------------
# _freeze/ stores executed cell output so a deploy/CI build (or a collaborator)
# can render the site WITHOUT re-running aggregate. That is the Quarto-recommended
# default, so it is intentionally NOT ignored here.
# Prefer not to track it (deploys then re-execute, needing the env)? Uncomment:
# /_freeze/
